IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `je54-nouns`

-- je54-vintage: which text of the Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954 governs on a given day.  The versions are DATA (the vintage table); the caller names a date and never a version.
-- Copyable (it imports only prelude, daydate and the nouns), with the commencement module and the definitions module.
--
-- What the sources show.  Seven texts are deposited, from 1 January 2019 (the first consolidated version on jerseylaw.je; the site offers nothing earlier).  Each text's days are the banner of its
-- .html ("Showing the law from ... to ...", repeated in its .meta.json).  The endnotes (the Table of Legislation History and the Table of Endnote References) name the amendment that made each change; they are
-- evidence for this table and are not provisions.  Before 1 January 2019 no text is deposited: the endnotes of the 2019 consolidation allow four provisions to be answered, by inference, from 28 March 2003
-- (Article 1(5), Article 1(6), and the Schedule definitions of "month" and "midnight"); every other provision refuses for a day before 1 January 2019, and for a day before 28 March 2003 so do those four.
--
-- The Table of Renumbered Provisions shows that Article 7 (service by post) was the original Article 12, Article 8 the original 13, and so on; that is why a question about service before 1 January 2019 refuses
-- (no text of those years is deposited, whatever the renumbering shows).

§ `The vintage table`

§§ `The days that matter`

