§§ `The citation of the Law (Article 18)`

-- Article 18 reads the same in all seven texts (checked by the coverage table generator, which compares the words after the endnote marks are removed).  It says by what name the Law may be cited; it makes no rule for anything else.
-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:83 | 18 Citation
-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:84 | This Law may be cited as the Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954.
-- src:78 | 18 Citation
-- src:79 | This Law may be cited as the Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954.
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Article 18 (src:l_17_1954_20210927:83-84), (src:78-79)
GIVETH A STRING
`the name by which Article 18 says the Law may be cited` MEANS "Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954"

§§ `The rows`

-- The days from 28 March 2003 to 31 December 2018: no text is deposited.  Only the four provisions that the V1 endnotes date to L.16/2003 are answered, by inference (see the header of this module).
-- Endnote [1] of V1: Article 1(5) amended by L.16/2003; [2]: Article 1(6) inserted by L.16/2003; [12]: the Schedule inserted by L.16/2003 and amended by L.8/2005, L.6/2010, L.4/2012, L.17/2015 and R&O.115/2016;
-- [13]: Part 1 of the Schedule amended by L.19/2018.  The Laws named in [12] and [13] are, by their titles, about other subjects (States of Jersey, pharmacists, civil partnership, dentists, young offenders,
-- marriage and civil status); that "month" and "midnight" are not among their changes is an inference.
