@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Endnotes, Table of Legislation History (src:137-209)
GIVETH A LIST OF `Row of the vintage table`
`the vintage table` MEANS
    LIST `row of the inferred text`,
         `row of the text V1`,
         `row of the text V2a`,
         `row of the text V2b`,
         `row of the text V2c`,
         `row of the text V2d`,
         `row of the text V2e`,
         `row of the text V2f`

§§ `The text in force on a day`

-- A named refusal (REFUSE at any type): there is no text of the Law for the day.  The wording is the one the brief fixes for every provision outside the four.
-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:1 | Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954
-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:2 | A LAW for promoting brevity and uniformity in enactments
-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:3 | Commencement [see endnotes]
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954 as consolidated for 1 January 2019 to 27 September 2021 (src:l_17_1954_20210927:1-3)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the Law has no deposited text for a day before the first consolidated version` MEANS
    REFUSE "before the first consolidated version (1 January 2019)"

@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Endnotes, Table of Legislation History, row L.17/1954 (src:137-139)
GIVEN a IS A TYPE
GIVETH AN a
`the vintage table leaves this day uncovered` MEANS
    REFUSE "the vintage table does not cover this day: this is a defect of the encoding, not an answer of the Law"

@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954 as consolidated: Endnotes (src:137-209)
GIVEN row IS A `Row of the vintage table`
      d IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the row of the vintage table governs` row d MEANS
        row's `first day` AT MOST d
    AND CONSIDER row's `last day`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
        WHEN JUST last THEN d AT MOST last

-- The text of the Law in force on a day, from the vintage table.  The selecting date of each Article is said in a comment at the function that reads it.
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Endnotes, Table of Legislation History (src:137-209)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Text of the Law`
`the text of the Law in force on` d MEANS
    BRANCH IF d LESS THAN `the day on which the Interpretation (Amendment) (Jersey) Law 2003 came into force`
           THEN `no text before 28 March 2003`
           OTHERWISE
               CONSIDER filter (GIVEN row YIELD `the row of the vintage table governs` row d) `the vintage table`
               WHEN row FOLLOWED BY rest THEN row's `which text`
               WHEN EMPTY THEN `the vintage table leaves this day uncovered`

-- The amendment (or the event) that made the text in force on a day the text in force, as the endnotes name it.
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Endnotes, Table of Legislation History (src:137-209)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A STRING
`the amendment that began the text of the Law in force on` d MEANS
    CONSIDER filter (GIVEN row YIELD `the row of the vintage table governs` row d) `the vintage table`
    WHEN row FOLLOWED BY rest THEN row's `amendment that began it`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN `the Law has no deposited text for a day before the first consolidated version`

-- The deposited file that shows the text in force on a day (its stem, beside RAW).
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954, Endnotes, Table of Legislation History (src:137-209)
GIVEN d IS A DATE
GIVETH A STRING
`the deposited file that shows the text of the Law in force on` d MEANS
    CONSIDER filter (GIVEN row YIELD `the row of the vintage table governs` row d) `the vintage table`
    WHEN row FOLLOWED BY rest THEN row's `source stem`
    WHEN EMPTY THEN `the Law has no deposited text for a day before the first consolidated version`

§§ `Which texts are deposited`

-- The seven deposited texts (V1 to V2f) are the only ones whose Articles can all be answered.  The inferred text answers four provisions only (Articles 1(5), 1(6), "month", "midnight"), and those are read
-- in je54-art01-commencement and je54-schedule-definitions; the other modules refuse unless the text is one of the seven.
-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:1 | Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954
-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:2 | A LAW for promoting brevity and uniformity in enactments
-- src:l_17_1954_20210927:3 | Commencement [see endnotes]
@ref Interpretation (Jersey) Law 1954 as consolidated for 1 January 2019 to 27 September 2021 (src:l_17_1954_20210927:1-3)
GIVEN v IS A `Text of the Law`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the text of the Law is one of the seven deposited texts` v MEANS
    CONSIDER v
    WHEN `no text before 28 March 2003` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the inferred text from 28 March 2003 to 31 December 2018` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE
